A||||4||Stroker||Best Performance Clutch?
Z||000000||Stroker||06-28-99||04:20 PM||||   Could anyone out there recommend a really good, strong clutch for use with the 3.2 liter upgrade?<br>  I want ALL the 200 hp getting to the wheels with NO slippage!<br>  All help is greatly appreciated!!<br>
Z||000001||batboy||06-28-99||06:37 PM||||In my opinion, the best high performance clutch on the market is the Centerforce. However, I'm not sure if there is one of these made for a Fiero.
Z||000002||Stroker||06-28-99||06:50 PM||||  batboy, I agree with you about the Centerforce clutch, they are great. However, I don't know either if they make one for the v-6.<br>    Can any one help on this?
Z||000003||mwbackus||06-28-99||08:24 PM||||Both the Centerforce Dual Friction and the standard centerforce are available for the 85-88 V6.  The advantages of the centerforce design are seen mostly at high rpm's, and therefore I highly recommend the dual friction disc due to the lower rpm operating ranges of the V6.  Any good heavy duty clutch with a Kevlar composite disc lining would also be an excellent choice and would more than meet the needs of a 200 hp engine.<p><br>Standard Centerforce         MS361914   ~$280<br>Dual Friction Centerforce    DF201914   ~$390<p>A variety of Heavy Duty Kevlar Composite clutches (Ram, Hays, etc.) are available, ranging from $250 to $350.<br>
Z||000004||theogre||06-28-99||10:58 PM||||visit www.centerforce.com<p>They will be happy to answer any question you may have about their product.<p>CenterForce product is available for ALL Fiero setups, but you may have to special order for things like V8.
